  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Energy Sector Management Capacity Strengthening - Energy Sector Manag</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Kapacitetutveckling MEM PFM</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d till MEM med capacitet h&#xf6;jande projekt f&#xf6;r planering och         management av energi sektor i Tanzania</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to MEM capacity for planning and management of the energy     sector in Tanzania</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the support is increased access to modern energy services through enhanced availability, reliability and affordability of energy supplies that are friendly to the environment. It is MEMs role to manage the energy sector through policy design, legislation and regulation supported by channeling of public financial resources to achieve that objective for the benefit of all Tanzanians. The project is a capacity building project that will support Ministry of Energy to better manage the energy sector.

For the Ministry of Energy (MoE) to have quality and reliable data and information, an Energy Information Management System (EIMS) is required. A strong Energy Information Management System requires institutional coordination among different parties in the energy sector as well as proper funding for a sustained capacity building of skilled people with relevant statistical and analytical tools to create and correlate the data at national level.

The main objective of Sida is to assist the Ministry of Energy (MoE) to create an elaborative energy information management system for all types of energy produced and consumed in Tanzania and to harmonize the data available in the region. This should be able to facilitate rapid transfer and exchange of information among regional countries. The Energy Information Management System is expected to be a bedrock of preparation of periodic National Energy Balances; Energy Demand Forecasting as well as Energy Supply Forecasting.</narrative>
  </description>
